    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A449B35167BB40706C055A54E4FB0DA/jobs/471689": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Instructional Designer (46959) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Instructional Designer (46959) Fully Remote   •   San Francisco - San Francisco, CA 94105 Apply Overview Salary Range $74,000.00 - $78,000.00 Salary/year Apply Description Golden Gate University · eLearning Instructional Designer Course Design Department eLearning Reports to Director, eLearning Schedule Full time, Pacific Time (PT) hours Location Remote (U.S.) Pay range $74,000 to $78,000 per year, based on experience About GGU Golden Gate University is the world's first AI-native, global, multilingual university: built for working adults, anchored in San Francisco at the heart of the AI economy. GGU was founded for working adults 125 years ago. Today every program teaches AI inside the discipline, so graduates use it as a tool of their trade. About the role You design and redevelop GGU courses and programs in D2L Brightspace and Edvisor.ai. Many are AI-graded and some are uncapped, so they need real interaction and depth. Your focus is active learning and regular and substantive interaction (RSI). When AI handles the grading, you work out where the instructor shows up, embed RSI into each course and design interactive content that is accessible from the start. You’ll join a collaborative remote team that brings a “yes, let’s figure out how” approach to solving problems. We draw on our skills, experience and creativity to work with faculty and university leadership to improve online learning and shape its future in the age of AI. This role calls for initiative, flexibility and persistence. Our team is growing, our processes are evolving, and responsibilities may shift as new needs emerge. You’ll contribute your expertise, support shared priorities and help develop how we work. If you enjoy turning ideas into action and building solutions with others, you’ll have a voice in what we create and how we get there. Key responsibilities Design and redevelop courses Design new courses and redevelop existing ones across D2L Brightspace and Edvisor.ai. Review existing courses and decide what to keep, revise, replace or retire. Develop new content, activities, assessments and faculty materials, even from limited sources. Outcomes and alignment Write course and weekly outcomes and topics, and align them with assessments and activities. Organize content into a clear, consistent weekly or modular structure. Interactive content and accessibility Design interactive content: discussions, live sessions, case work and peer activities. Apply WCAG 2.1 AA and UDL so every student has equitable access and more than one way to engage. Regular and substantive interaction (RSI) Embed RSI in every course, even when AI handles the grading. Find and test new ways for faculty to interact with students in AI-graded and uncapped courses. Give faculty presence tools, such as feedback templates, weekly touchpoints and office hours plans. Course builds and quality Use generative AI in design and development, and validate every AI draft. Build and maintain courses in Brightspace and Edvisor.ai using GGU templates and design standards. Review courses for usability, accessibility and quality before launch. Troubleshoot course-level issues and coordinate with LMS support when needed. Faculty, evaluation and team Partner with faculty and subject matter experts on course goals, content and priorities. Evaluate courses with student, assessment and engagement data, and recommend improvements. Manage multiple projects and deadlines, and help write and update our SOPs. Other related duties as assigned. Qualifications What you bring Required Five or more years of instructional design experience, preferably in higher education. Teaching experience, ideally at the college level. Experience designing aligned online courses with active learning and interactive content. Working knowledge of RSI, accessibility standards including WCAG 2.1 AA, and UDL. Hands-on D2L Brightspace experience, including building courses on your own. Demonstrated use of generative AI in design, and the judgment to validate its output. Strong collaboration, writing and visual communication skills. Strong organization and project management across multiple courses and deadlines. Works well on a small remote team, sharing what you learn and pitching in where needed. Flexible as a new team learns together and builds its processes as it goes. Master’s degree in instructional design, educational technology, education or a related field. Preferred A second graduate degree or a doctorate. Edvisor.ai or other AI platform experience, and large or uncapped online courses. Quality Matters or formal QA experience, and online programs for working adults. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A449B35167BB40706C055A54E4FB0DA/jobs/470196": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Program Coordinator (46813) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Program Coordinator (46813) Hybrid   •   San Francisco - San Francisco, CA 94105 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,304.00 - $70,304.00 Salary/year Apply Description Position Title: Program Coordinator Department Name: GGU Worldwide Position Reports To: Associate Director of Administration and Partner Support, GGU WW FLSA STATUS : Salaried Salary Range: $70,304.00 Benefits: The University's comprehensive benefits program Days & Hours: Monday through Friday, 37.5 hours per week. The standard work schedule is 9:00 am to 5:30 pm, maybe adjusted.  A flexible schedule may require evening and weekend hours. BASIC FUNCTION AND SCOPE: The Program Coordinator provides timely, high-level administrative and academic support to GGU Worldwide’s Deans and Faculty Directors. This position is responsible for supporting the day-to-day administrative and coordinative operations of various international partner programs, requiring strong attention to detail, excellent interpersonal skills, cross-cultural communication, technical and AI skills, a commitment to student-centered service, academic quality assurance, and accreditor compliance. The role demands the ability to multi-task and adapt to varied responsibilities and time zones across GGU Worldwide programs, stakeholders, platforms, and geographies. The Program Coordinator provides dedicated administrative and logistical support to GGU Worldwide’s partnerships. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Work collaboratively as part of the GGU Worldwide administrative team to deliver timely, quality, and focused care and support to students, faculty, staff, and partners. Assist Faculty Directors with course scheduling, syllabi management, instructor selection, student evaluations, timesheet tracking, record keeping, and other academic operations. Support Faculty Directors with pre-admission, enrollment, verification, course enrollment, attendance monitoring, student standards status, WASC reports, translation/interpretation, and academic quality initiatives and etc. Use platforms such as Curriculog to support curriculum changes and Smartsheet to manage course schedules. Serve as the point of contact for partner adjunct faculty onboarding, support, and coordination. Assist Dean and Associate Dean with special projects and doctoral programs. Assure GGU Worldwide courses and programs in the GGU Catalog, all websites, and social media pages, and marketing materials are up to date. Course schedule planning, coordination, confirmation, and oversight. Help Faculty Director and Deans monitor faculty-student course engagement. Coordinate with other university departments, including Student accounts, Division of Student Success, facilities, schools, among others. Assist deans, faculty directors and faculty on outreach, partner relations, and students’ associations. Schedule and coordinate appointments and meetings; utilize strong judgment in managing priorities of requests and escalating as necessary for resolution and/or prioritization. Prepare documents, reports, agendas, presentations, and related materials. Assist with on campus and off campus events, orientations, immersions, commencement, and other activities. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Education requirement: Bachelor's degree; Master’s degree a plus Years of experience: Two to five years’ experience in academic program support role or similar is preferred. Knowledge of: English and other languages is preferred but not required. Curriculog, Salesforce, Colleague, and Smartsheet are preferred but not required. AI tools, LinkedIn, and short messaging apps including WhatsApp, WeChat, Viber. Direct job-related requirements: Familiarity with CRM and learning management systems High level of proficiency with modern office practices, procedures, equipment, and software, including Microsoft Office Suite, Zoom, MS Teams and other office technology. Skills and abilities: Ability to work on-site at the San Francisco, California campus. Ability to work off-site activities including but not limited to immersions, study tours, community events. Strong interpersonal and bilingual skills with the ability to maintain positive and professional relationships with students, faculty, staff, and partners. Ability to work in a multicultural, diverse, and inclusive environment. Excellent interpersonal, administrative, communication, and organizational skills. Outstanding command of the English language in written and verbal forms. Ability to effectively interpret, organize, and present information and ideas in writing. Excellent project management skills, including ability to simultaneously manage several projects and activities, as well as use AI tools. Work effectively both as a leader and as a team member to support departmental goals, providing assistance across programs while consistently prioritizing the best interests of students and graduates. Supplemental Information To apply: Please go to http://www.ggu.edu/jobs to submit an application, letter of interest, and a resume. In applying for a position, candidates sign a consent authorizing a broader inquiry which may include reference checks, a motor vehicle check, and a third-party background check. Golden Gate University is an equal employment opportunity employer. We support inclusive excellence and are committed to creating a safe and welcoming community for all. University policy prohibits discrimination based on race, color, religion/creed, national origin, ancestry, age, sex/gender, sexual orientation, marital status, medical condition, physical or mental disability, gender stereotyping, and gender identity, gender expression, military or veteran status, taking a protected leave (e.g., family medical or pregnancy leave), or on any other basis protected by applicable laws. The University has a strong commitment to the principles of diversity and inclusion, and to maintaining working and learning environments that reinforces these practices. The University welcomes and encourages applications from all demographics. Circa Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A449B35167BB40706C055A54E4FB0DA/jobs/471810": {
      "title": "School Certifying Official",
      "description": "School Certifying Official (46962) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account School Certifying Official (46962) Fully Remote   •   San Francisco - San Francisco, CA 94105 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,304.00 - $75,000.00 Salary/year Apply Description School Certifying Official (SCO) Job Title: School Certifying Official Reports To: Associate Director of Student Financial Services Department: Student Financial Services Salary: $70,304 - $75,000 Location: Remote Position Summary Under the direction of and reporting to the Associate Director, a School Certifying Official (SCO) works with our team of SCOs to ensures GGU complies with U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) regulations and process enrollment certifications, monitor academic progress, and act as a critical liaison between student veterans and the VA to guarantee uninterrupted educational benefits. Each SCO is responsible for a designated cohort of students Key Responsibilities Benefit Certification: Evaluate student schedules and degree audits, then accurately submit enrollment certifications to the VA via their digital platforms. Compliance & Auditing: Maintain deep familiarity with all VA education benefit chapters (e.g., Post-9/11 GI Bill, Montgomery GI Bill, VR&E) to ensure institutional compliance and prevent financial overpayments. Student Advising: Counsel student veterans on benefit eligibility, required paperwork, and military tuition assistance. Academic Monitoring: Track the academic progress, enrollment changes, and graduation status of VA-funded students, promptly reporting any adjustments to the VA. Cross-Department Collaboration: Partner with Financial Aid, Student Accounts, and Academic Advising to ensure student files are complete and institutional reporting standards are met. Qualifications Qualifications & Skills Experience and Education: Bachelor’s degree, minimum of 2–3 years of experience in higher education, preferably within a Registrar's Office, Financial Aid, or Veterans Affairs department or a combination of education and related experience. Compliance Knowledge: Direct, hands-on experience using VA-ONCE or the modern VA Enrollment Manager system is strongly preferred. Communication: Exceptional organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills to guide non-traditional students and manage confidential data securely. Service Excellence: Dedicated to delivering high-quality, responsive customer service to the university community. Workload: High-volume periods occur prior to and during the start of academic terms (e.g., January, April/May and August/September). Supplemental Information To apply: Please go to http://www.ggu.edu/jobs to submit an application, letter of interest, and a resume. In applying for a position, candidates sign a consent authorizing a broader inquiry which may include reference checks, a motor vehicle check, and a third-party background check. Golden Gate University is an equal employment opportunity employer. We support inclusive excellence and are committed to creating a safe and welcoming community for all. University policy prohibits discrimination based on race, color, religion/creed, national origin, ancestry, age, sex/gender, sexual orientation, marital status, medical condition, physical or mental disability, gender stereotyping, and gender identity, gender expression, military or veteran status, taking a protected leave (e.g., family medical or pregnancy leave), or on any other basis protected by applicable laws. The University has a strong commitment to the principles of diversity and inclusion, and to maintaining working and learning environments that reinforces these practices. The University welcomes and encourages applications from all demographics. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/1A449B35167BB40706C055A54E4FB0DA/jobs/474439": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Instructional Designer (47033) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Instructional Designer (47033) Fully Remote   •   San Francisco - San Francisco, CA 94105 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,304.00 - $78,000.00 Salary/year Apply Description Instructional Designer Course Design & Learning Effectiveness Department eLearning Salary range $70,304–$78,000 annually Reports to Director of Learning Design, Assessment, and Emerging Technology Schedule Full time · Pacific Time working hours Location Remote (U.S.) Compensation: Placement within the posted salary range is based on relevant experience, demonstrated skills, evidence of work quality, and alignment with the position’s responsibilities. Candidates who demonstrate exceptional proficiency in advanced course design, assessment alignment, higher education teaching, faculty collaboration, and development of engaging online learning experiences may be considered for the upper end of the range. Meeting preferred qualifications does not automatically guarantee maximum pay. About the role Design and redevelop engaging, academically rigorous online courses and related curricula in Brightspace, Edvisor.ai, and other supported environments. Partner with faculty to align outcomes, activities, assessments, and regular and substantive interaction (RSI), including in AI-supported and large-enrollment courses. How we work Our instructional designers work closely with faculty and colleagues from initial course concepts through launch and improvement. We share responsibility for problem-solving, step into emerging program and curriculum projects, and make thoughtful design decisions even when source materials or processes are still evolving. Key responsibilities Course and assessment design Partner with faculty to design or revise courses, translating source materials into clear, coherent course design documents. Align outcomes, weekly topics, content, activities, and assessments; identify what existing material to retain or improve. Create active-learning experiences, including discussions, cases, and collaborative or peer activities. Faculty presence and learning quality Design regular and substantive interaction (RSI) and practical faculty-presence strategies, including in AI-graded courses. Apply Universal Design for Learning, accessibility, and inclusive teaching practices throughout course design. Evaluate course effectiveness using learner feedback, assessment results, engagement data, and quality reviews. Course development and collaboration Build, update, and test courses in Brightspace, Edvisor.ai, and other tools; critically review AI-generated content. Collaborate with teammates on multimedia, technology integration, accessibility, quality assurance, and launches. Provide one-off faculty assistance, including activity testing and support for instructional challenges. Contribute to parallel programs, coordinated curriculum, reusable learning resources, and other shared projects. Qualifications What you bring Required Five or more years of instructional design experience and a master’s degree in instructional design, education, educational technology, or a related field. Higher education teaching experience, including direct responsibility for instruction of college or university students. Demonstrated ability to design online courses with aligned outcomes, assessments, active learning, and meaningful faculty-student interaction. Hands-on D2L Brightspace course-building experience and working knowledge of RSI, UDL, and WCAG accessibility standards. Effective use of generative AI in course development, including critical review of accuracy and instructional quality. Strong writing, faculty collaboration, project management, and judgment across concurrent deadlines. Preferred Doctorate or second graduate degree; Edvisor.ai or similar AI learning-platform experience. Experience with adult learners, high-enrollment courses, Quality Matters, or formal course quality assurance. Experience with parallel programs, curriculum mapping, or coordinated program pathways. Professional proficiency in written Spanish. Supplemental Information To apply: Please go to http://www.ggu.edu/jobs to submit an application, letter of interest, and a resume. In applying for a position, candidates sign a consent authorizing a broader inquiry which may include reference checks, a motor vehicle check, and a third-party background check. Golden Gate University is an equal employment opportunity employer. We support inclusive excellence and are committed to creating a safe and welcoming community for all. University policy prohibits discrimination based on race, color, religion/creed, national origin, ancestry, age, sex/gender, sexual orientation, marital status, medical condition, physical or mental disability, gender stereotyping, and gender identity, gender expression, military or veteran status, taking a protected leave (e.g., family medical or pregnancy leave), or on any other basis protected by applicable laws. The University has a strong commitment to the principles of diversity and inclusion, and to maintaining working and learning environments that reinforces these practices. The University welcomes and encourages applications from all demographics. Circa Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
